{"title":"Diagnostics","description":"Collect logs, configuration and system details from a Stirling PDF Docker container into one archive for troubleshooting or a bug report.","unlisted":false,"space":"server","layout":"","article":"<a class=\"doc-space\" data-accent=\"server\" href=\"/Server/\"><svg class=\"icon\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"3\" y=\"14\" width=\"18\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M7 6.5h.01M7 17.5h.01\"/></svg><span>Self-hosted server</span></a>\n    <h1>Diagnostics</h1>\n<p>The Docker images include a diagnostics tool that gathers logs, configuration, system information and app metrics into one archive. Attach it when you report a problem; see the <a href=\"/Tools/FAQ/\">FAQ</a> for where to get help.</p>\n<h2 id=\"run-the-tool\" class=\"anchor-heading\">Run the tool<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#run-the-tool\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><div class=\"codeblock\"><div class=\"codeblock-head\"><span class=\"codeblock-lang\">bash</span><button class=\"codeblock-copy\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg></button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">docker</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> exec</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -it</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">container_nam</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">e</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">></span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> diag</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The tool needs an interactive terminal, so keep the <code>-it</code> flags.</p>\n<p>Choose a mode when prompted:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1) Auto</strong> collects the last day of logs, <code>/configs</code>, system information, and the app's status, health and metrics endpoints. It does not redact anything.</li>\n<li><strong>2) Custom</strong> asks what to include and whether to redact.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>PDFs, images and archives are never collected.</p>\n<h3 id=\"custom-mode-options\" class=\"anchor-heading\">Custom mode options<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#custom-mode-options\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h3><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Prompt</th>\n<th>Default</th>\n<th>Collects</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Output directory</td>\n<td><code>/configs</code></td>\n<td>Where to save the archive.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Days of logs to include</td>\n<td><code>1</code></td>\n<td>Log files from this many days.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Include /configs?</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Configuration files, such as <code>settings.yml</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Include /customFiles (excluding PDFs)?</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Your custom files.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Include /pipeline (excluding PDFs)?</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Pipeline working files.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Include /tmp/stirling-pdf?</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Temporary processing files.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Include system information?</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>OS, CPU, memory, disk, Java and Python versions.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Include environment variables?</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Every environment variable.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fetch app status/health/metrics endpoints?</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Status, health and load data.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Include /api/v1/ui-data endpoints?</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Data the app's sign, pipeline and OCR screens use.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Redact sensitive information from diagnostics?</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Then asks separately about secrets, tokens and passwords (default yes), URL hosts, email addresses, and host, domain and server fields (default no).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"admonition admonition-caution\"><div class=\"admonition-heading\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0zM12 9v4M12 17h.01\"/></svg><span>Caution</span></div><div class=\"admonition-content\">\n<p>Configuration files and environment variables can contain passwords and keys. Before sharing a bundle publicly, for example in a GitHub issue, run Custom mode with redaction on and check the archive yourself: redaction can miss values.</p>\n</div></div>\n<h2 id=\"get-the-archive\" class=\"anchor-heading\">Get the archive<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#get-the-archive\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><p>The tool prints the archive path when it finishes, in a <code>Created tar.gz</code> line. Copy it out of the container:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><div class=\"codeblock-head\"><span class=\"codeblock-lang\">bash</span><button class=\"codeblock-copy\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg></button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">docker</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> cp</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">container_nam</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">e</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">></span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">:/configs/stirling-diagnostics-20260917-120000.tar.gz</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> ./</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The archive holds <code>summary.txt</code> (what was collected, and the version) and a <code>bundle/</code> folder with the collected files.</p>\n<h2 id=\"aot-diagnostics\" class=\"anchor-heading\">AOT diagnostics<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#aot-diagnostics\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><p>If you run with ahead-of-time compilation on (<code>STIRLING_AOT_ENABLE=true</code>), <code>aot-diag</code> (or <code>aot-diagnostics</code>) checks why the AOT cache fails to build, which mostly happens on ARM64. It checks cache integrity and JVM compatibility and can run smoke tests:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><div class=\"codeblock-head\"><span class=\"codeblock-lang\">bash</span><button class=\"codeblock-copy\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg></button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">docker</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> exec</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -it</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">container_nam</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">e</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">></span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> aot-diag</span></span></code></pre></div>\n\n    <div class=\"doc-source\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/Stirling-Tools/Stirling-Tools.github.io/edit/main/docs/Server/Operations/Diagnostics.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n        <svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M17 3a2.83 2.83 0 1 1 4 4L7.5 20.5 2 22l1.5-5.5L17 3z\"/></svg>\n        Edit this page on GitHub\n      </a>\n    </div>","toc":"<div class=\"toc-title\">On this page</div><ul><li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#run-the-tool\">Run the tool</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l3\"><a href=\"#custom-mode-options\">Custom mode options</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#get-the-archive\">Get the archive</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#aot-diagnostics\">AOT diagnostics</a></li></ul>","pager":"<a class=\"pager-link pager-prev\" href=\"/Server/Operations/Usage-Monitoring/\">\n        <span class=\"pager-dir\">&larr; Previous</span>\n        <span class=\"pager-title\">Usage monitoring</span>\n      </a><a class=\"pager-link pager-next\" href=\"/Server/AI/\">\n        <span class=\"pager-dir\">Next &rarr;</span>\n        <span class=\"pager-title\">Overview</span>\n      </a>"}